---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CopyCommand from '../components/copyCommand';
import { githubUrl, skillInstallCommand, skillUseCommand } from '../lib/nav';
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';

const skillUrl = `${githubUrl}/blob/HEAD/skills/lattice/SKILL.md`;

const contents = [
	{
		file: 'SKILL.md',
		blurb:
			'Where Lattice finds workspaces, tasks and dependencies, what does not exist in lattice.json, how to run and preview tasks, and how to move a 1.x config with lattice migrate.',
	},
	{
		file: 'references/configuration.md',
		blurb: 'Every lattice.json field, its type, its default, and the error it raises when it is wrong.',
	},
	{
		file: 'references/cli.md',
		blurb: 'Every command and flag, the exit codes, the environment variables, and which of them wins.',
	},
	{
		file: 'references/toolchains.md',
		blurb: 'How a workspace\'s tool is chosen, the tasks each tool can run, the engines that can be checked by name, and what a failed check says.',
	},
	{
		file: 'references/troubleshooting.md',
		blurb: 'Symptom, cause, and fix for the failures a run produces.',
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="For agents · Lattice"
	description="Install the Lattice skill so your coding agent knows how to read a lattice.json, run tasks, and work out why a run failed."
>
	<section class="px-3 pt-5 pb-4">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h1 class="fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.75rem); letter-spacing: -0.03em;">
				For agents
			</h1>
			<p class="fs-5 mb-0" style="color: var(--text-muted);">
				A coding agent's training data predates Lattice, so it has no working knowledge of it. Ask one
				to edit a <code>lattice.json</code> and it lists every workspace by hand, invents keys, and
				guesses at commands, because that is what the config files it has seen look like. This skill
				gives it the real commands, fields, and error messages instead.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-3 pb-5">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-3">Install the skill</h2>
			<CopyCommand client:visible command={skillInstallCommand} />
			<p class="mt-3 mb-4" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.65;">
				Run it in the repo you want the skill in. The CLI finds the coding agents you have installed and
				writes the skill where each of them looks for it. It records what it wrote in
				<code>skills-lock.json</code>.
			</p>

			<h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-3">Load it for one session instead</h2>
			<CopyCommand client:visible command={skillUseCommand} />
			<p class="mt-3 mb-0" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.65;">
				This prints the skill as a prompt and writes nothing to disk. Use it for a one-off task, or for
				an agent the installer doesn't know about.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-3 pb-5">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-3">What's in the skill</h2>
			<p class="mb-4" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.65;">
				One instruction file, plus four references the agent reads only when a task needs them. The list
				below is the whole skill.
			</p>
			<div class="list-group list-group-flush">
				{
					contents.map((item) => (
						<div class="list-group-item px-0 py-3" style="background: transparent; border-color: var(--border-subtle);">
							<code class="d-block mb-1" style="color: var(--text); font-size: 0.85rem;">
								{item.file}
							</code>
							<span class="d-block" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.6;">
								{item.blurb}
							</span>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</div>
			<p class="mt-4 mb-0" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.65;">
				The source lives in the repo at
				<a href={skillUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>skills/lattice/SKILL.md</code></a>.
				Read it before you install it. It is plain Markdown, and it is the same text your agent acts on.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="px-3 pb-5">
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-3">Without the skill</h2>
			<p class="mb-0" style="color: var(--text-subtle); line-height: 1.65;">
				An agent that can read files and run commands gets most of the way on its own. Have it run
				<code>lattice run &lt;task&gt; --dry-run</code> before reading anything: most of what Lattice
				runs is not in <code>lattice.json</code>, and the dry run lists every workspace and every
				resolved command without running one. For flags,
				<code>lattice --help</code> and each subcommand's <code>--help</code> are authoritative. The
				<a href={withBase('/docs/configuration')}>configuration</a> and
				<a href={withBase('/docs/cli')}>CLI</a> pages cover the same ground, and every page on this site
				is Markdown in the repo.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
